WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.360
[music playing]

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.960
One, two, one two three four!

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:19.560
[music playing]

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.260
I remember when I was a young man my

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.040
momma took me to the store and I was

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.120
scared out of my mind as I

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.980
stared at that dressing room door

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:29.480
I was like

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.540
what if the pants are too bright too dark

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.440
too baggy too light too big

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.740
wrong cut or too tight

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.460
and mom was like "just be yourself son"

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.820
whatever you choose'll be right

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.320
WELL

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.920
It's like she knew my very soul 'cause

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.340
the pants I bought that day would change my life

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.400
I left that store with a uniform that I was wearing

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.180
when I met my wife and

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.640
at my first punk rock show

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.120
and when I touched my first boob

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.340
and the first time I read Thoreau

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.460
I did it all in my

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:00.520
t-shirt and jeans

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.280
that's right, it doesn't mean

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.820
anything

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.100
people who know me know

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.640
that I try not to say too much just with my clothes

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.760
and if you wanna get to know me, man

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.420
we're gonna have to talk

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.620
so that you can find out who I am

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.940
t-shirt and jeans

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.740
[more music]

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.140
well jeans are prety great they're

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.820
durable and comfortable

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.040
they're pants made out of plants

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.180
so it's hard to argue they're unethical

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:30.280
and a shirt can say a little or a lot

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.220
I'm a fan of unironic images of things I like

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.160
like giraffes or my YouTube friends

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:35.960
or bands

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:36.820
or chickens

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.140
Jesus, nerds, or bikes

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:40.520
But if you really wanna know what I love

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.580
most about this wardrobe

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.080
Is that it tells you very little

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.780
about what lies beneath these clothes

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.000
just by looking at me

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.960
You would never know if I'm a

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.680
thousandaire or a billionare

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.180
I wanna tell you with my mouth

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:58.020
not with the clothes I wear

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.500
well I think it's odd how when we rebel

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.520
we put on uniforms

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.200
like eye-liner or fancy pants

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.120
that come factory pre-torn

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.260
it's easy to say

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:17.000
that a guy must be a certain way

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.880
just because he dresses off-beat

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.880
and a sub-cultural short-cut

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.480
might be what he's going for but

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:30.960
it's always gonna be incomplete

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.680
yeah, we're never really ever gonna know

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.120
what that means

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.320
which is why I wear

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.620
t-shirt and jeans

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.440
that's right, it doesn't mean

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.700
anything

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.100
people who know me know

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.700
that I try not to say too much just with my clothes

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.720
and if you wanna get to know me, man

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.320
we're gonna have to talk

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.600
so that you can find out who I am

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.360
we're gonna have to talk so that you can find out who I am

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:07.300
yeah we're gonna have to talk so that you can find out who I am

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.600
well we're gonna have to talk so that you can find out who I am

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.140
John, we're going on tour.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.340
We're starting in Kansas and going a bunch of places in Texas

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.980
and then across Arizona and up California

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.380
It's a pretty short tour, just 10 days.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:22.100
We're touring with Wheezy Waiter's band, the Driftless Pony Club, and Harry and the Potters,

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.820
who have probably the best live show I've ever seen

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.960
The shows are fun and laid back and we do our best

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.840
to pack them full of interesting stuff.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.080
Hank Green and the Perfect Strangers go on last

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.740
but I sort of MC the whole evening. It's very fun.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.460
Tickets are on sale now for all of it except El Paso

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.440
I'm sorry, El Paso. We'll figure it out, though, and I'll let you know.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.720
We'll have some great merch: shirts and posters and a flash drive that contains every song I've ever written on it,

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:46.680
and if you pay in cash we'll do our best to give you your change including a $2 bill that I have signed.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.840
'Cause that's weird.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.940
We have a great time and all these people on Twitter agree!

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:53.640
I got some testimonials - just searched "Hank Green concert"

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.440
It's fun, come along!

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.195
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

